# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
$ABI strict
$Module cookie_handoff 3 "Request-owned response cookie handoff"
$Event delivery_event

$Function VOID reset(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_recv

Discard request state before a new receive attempt, including restart to a HIT.

$Function STRING open(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_miss

Allocate a handoff owned by this client task, including task-finalization cleanup.

$Function VOID bind(PRIV_TASK, STRING key)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Bind the backend task before removing the internal key from the origin request.

$Function VOID discard(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_error

Discard fields belonging to an abandoned backend response.

$Function BOOL detach(PRIV_TASK, STRING rules, BOOL background = 0)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Detach complete Set-Cookie fields only when every name has the Shared action.
Rules are ordered action TAB kind TAB literal-name LF, generated by the same
resolver used for request cookies. Personal values never enter the cache object.

$Function VOID deliver(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Append the original fields to their owning client response only.

$Function INT pending()

Number of live handoffs, for lifecycle verification (never cookie contents).

$Function BOOL mutation_backend_start(PRIV_TASK, STRING site, STRING native_policy, STRING credential)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Called at the normal UltraCache dynamic backend boundary after negotiation.
Own a request-bound revoke-only receipt context on the existing backend task.
Unknown identity provenance unbinds only its registered application scope.

$Function BOOL mutation_backend_response(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Validate a receipt against this exact backend
execution, revoke authority before browser headers, strip its transport fields.
Never grant CLEAN or change application status, body or Set-Cookie on failure.

$Function BOOL execution_drain_available(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
$Restrict vcl_synth

Accepted execution-drain dispatch negotiation for this exact application scope.

$Function INT execution_drain_authorize(PRIV_TASK, STRING site, STRING native_policy, STRING credential)
$Restrict vcl_recv

Authenticate a strict producer dispatch and bind it to the existing client owner.
Returns HTTP status, never an execution completion or cache admission.

$Function INT execution_drain_backend(PRIV_TASK, STRING credential)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Return 1 for an owned metadata backend, 0 for ordinary, -1 for unavailable owner.

$Function INT execution_drain_response(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Return 1 for valid diagnostic 204, 0 for ordinary, -1 for invalid metadata reply.

$Function INT delivery_recv(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_recv

UltraCache only: 1 prepare PASS, 2 prepared fragment synth, -1 abort, 0 ordinary.
The phase is request-owned, never inferred from client headers.

$Function INT delivery_held_miss(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_miss

Only the same top-request's owned held-read lookup may return 1 to restart.
Returns 0 for ordinary misses and -1 for an invalid held-read reservation.

$Function INT delivery_held_waiters()
$Restrict vcl_synth vcl_deliver

Read-only count of owned requests actually on the engine HSH waiting list.

$Function BOOL delivery_guard(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_pass vcl_miss

Reject a post-prepare parent refetch instead of executing its provider twice.

$Function BOOL delivery_resume_authorized(PRIV_TOP, STRING site)
$Restrict vcl_recv

Read-only ingress proof for the same initially authorized top-level GET.
Requires exact native phase/restart plus stored adapter site, host and URI.
No request header, positive restart count alone or other task creates a grant.

$Function BOOL delivery_recover(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_miss

Use one authenticated public-publication-only recovery fetch after an owned
prepare whose response explicitly confirmed that application capability.

$Function BOOL delivery_backend(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Bind the single owned prepare request and set its origin wire from native state.

$Function BOOL delivery_public_source_backend(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Apply the owning continuation's real source URI/public Cookie wire before its
execution context is signed. No caller header can create the source phase.

$Function BOOL selection_public_source(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
$Restrict vcl_synth

Negotiated source-only public parent role on the existing selection owner.

$Function BOOL selection_public_projection(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
$Restrict vcl_synth

Negotiated actual public tuple/resolver outcome on the same selection owner.

$Function STRING delivery_public_source_outcome(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_deliver vcl_synth

Request-local source diagnostic only, never cached parent or admission metadata.

$Function BOOL delivery_capture(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Capture authentic repeated Set-Cookie and attach the body fetch filter.
The caller must use uc_delivery_capture with do_stream=false and private PASS.

$Function BACKEND delivery_local_backend(PRIV_TASK, PRIV_VCL)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Select the native source only for an owned, prepared request snapshot recovery.
Returns no backend for ordinary requests, Basic or application snapshot fallback.

$Function BOOL delivery_local_source(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Select the request snapshot source filter before the ordinary native ESI parser.

$Function BACKEND delivery_private_backend(PRIV_TASK, PRIV_VCL)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Select a scoped fragment source only from the authenticated prepared claim.

$Function BOOL delivery_private_source()
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Identify a backend task which owns the prepared private fragment source.

$Function INT delivery_private_remaining()
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Whole remaining seconds for an authenticated read-only private cache lookup.

$Function BOOL delivery_recovery_response(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Validate the bound snapshot-only response before stripping its ephemeral proof.

$Function INT delivery_deliver(PRIV_TOP, STRING target, INT occurrences, BOOL begin = 0)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

UltraCache only: begin an eligible parent HIT prepare, or validate/restore its
captured response. 1 means restart before headers, -1 means abort. A completed
whole-document alternative returns 2 for immediate owned private synthesis.
A fragment continuation appends authentic provider fields and returns 0 for final delivery.
Only begin=true may start a new continuation; resumed deliveries still receive
the actual parent metadata even when the parent was fetched after eviction.

$Function STRING delivery_outcome(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_deliver vcl_synth

Request-owned verified/degraded/unverified outcome after complete authenticated
prepare and final delivery validation. Never reads a cached parent health field.
An ordinary late ESI child or missing/invalid producer outcome stays unverified.

$Function BOOL delivery_synth(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_synth

Replay an owned complete private document or pre-rendered private child.

$Function STRING selection_epoch()

Registry-lifetime identity including the native build; no visitor data. Changes
after a worker/registry restart and stays stable across overlapping VCL loads.

$Function BOOL selection_register(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope, STRING wordpress_policy, STRING names, BOOL enabled, STRING guest_policy = "")
$Restrict vcl_recv

Called only after existing per-site HTTP capabilities authentication. Stores
the required frontend scope, exact resolver names and WP identity, never values.
An empty names list is an application boundary without an active resolver.
Enabled false removes only that exact scope. Ordinary probes do not call it.

$Function STRING selection_names(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_synth

Return registered metadata only for this adapter site, host and exact scope.

$Function STRING selection_wordpress_policy(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_synth

Return the independent accepted WP policy identity.

$Function STRING selection_actions(STRING rules, STRING names)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_miss vcl_synth

Project exact names through the active generated ordered matcher. Existing
unmatched-name behavior is Shared; no additional cookie decision list.

$Function INT selection_begin(PRIV_TOP, STRING site, STRING policy, STRING rules, BOOL cold = 0, BOOL reselect = 0)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_miss

After normal route/auth/cookie decisions: 1 owned original-route preparation,
0 no applicable negotiated boundary at this stage, -1 allocation/binding error.
Early receive resolves active provider variants. Cold MISS prepares a registered
non-resolver boundary without turning a warm plain HIT into an application call.

$Function BOOL selection_cold(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_hash

Whether this validated selected parent belongs to the ordinary cold-lookup key.
Its manifest still binds rendering, but does not create a separate publication
namespace which would require an application call to rediscover on every HIT.

$Function STRING selection_manifest(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_hash vcl_hit vcl_deliver

Only an owned prepared selection exposes its exact signed target publication.

$Function STRING selection_variant(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_recv

Native Variant projection of the logical candidate; actual Cookie stays intact.

$Function BOOL selection_local(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

True only for the new authenticated selected-publication source. Old recovery
keeps its own cookie variation and source-manifest binding unchanged.

$Function BOOL selection_raw(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

True only for an owned public-select fetch returning a genuine non-protocol
response. Deliver that private PASS normally, without capturing its body.

$Function STRING delivery_retire(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Exact site/host/URL/old-publication ban expression after a verified early conflict.

$Function BOOL delivery_reselect_pending(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_recv

Same owner may re-enter current policy selection only after its single early conflict.

$Function BOOL delivery_conflict_response(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Validate early conflict proof before removing its ephemeral request bindings.

$Function VOID guest_ingress()
$Restrict vcl_recv

Capture original absent Cookie/Authorization before normalization; no continuation.

$Function VOID guest_select(STRING site, STRING policy)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_miss

Select registered complete guest namespace for the native-owned first-visit predicate.

$Function BOOL guest_warm_parent(STRING site, STRING policy, STRING credential)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_miss

Validate a request-bound ordinary refill proof before selecting the existing
private-capable parent namespace. No cookies, registry or origin fields change.

$Function BOOL guest_warm_parent_result()
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Current top-level delivery selected the parent with an authenticated Warm proof.
This observation is request-owned, never cached parent metadata.

$Function STRING guest_key()
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_hash vcl_hit vcl_deliver

Current request-owned guest namespace, never a browser cookie classification.

$Function BOOL guest_result()
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Complete guest object provenance matches the selected request namespace.

$Function STRING selection_guest_policy(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_synth

Read the accepted exact-scope guest declaration without changing registration.

$Function STRING guest_issuer_authorization(STRING credential, STRING canonical)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Domain-separated HMAC of the actual POST method, forwarded Host, raw URI and
native canonical context. The reusable credential is not forwarded to PHP.

$Function BOOL delivery_reuse_available()
$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_deliver vcl_synth

Experimental resolver build capability, not negotiated producer reuse support.
False unless the exact engine-source build receipt was explicitly supplied.

$Function BOOL reuse_register(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope, STRING native_policy, STRING wordpress_policy, STRING reuse_policy, BOOL enabled, STRING coverage_policy = "")
$Restrict vcl_recv

Authenticated capabilities only. New authority starts UNBOUND. Disabling and
policy changes revoke scope readiness without forgetting outstanding writers.

$Function INT reuse_control(PRIV_TASK, STRING site, STRING native_policy)
$Restrict vcl_recv

Called only inside adapter site-token control authentication. Native metadata
operations return HTTP status and request-owned JSON; no ordinary fill grants
clean authority. Context creates only UNBOUND tag slots.

$Function BOOL reuse_control_synth(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_synth

Deliver the current authenticated operation JSON without response workspace caps.

$Function INT delivery_reuse_resolve(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Experimental existing-owner pre-header resolution of authenticated descriptor
claims: -1 unavailable/invalid owner, 0 dependencies missing, 1 all pinned.
Does not create admission, authorize cached delivery or bypass prepare.

$Function INT delivery_reuse_count(PRIV_TOP, BOOL hits)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Request-local descriptor counts for isolated qualification; not body occurrence
counts and not a cache-authority assertion.

$Function BOOL delivery_reuse_materialize(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Copy reserved HIT bytes into the existing owner for selective context/replay,
preserving native absolute expiry. Production VCL does not call these methods.

$Function STRING delivery_reuse_finalize_context(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_deliver

Experimental signed compact context from the actual owned candidate/selected
parent and original input evidence. NULL declines only this optimization; it
does not install admission or grant a full composed HIT.

$Function BOOL delivery_reuse_pending(PRIV_TOP)
$Restrict vcl_miss

True only for an actual owned metadata lookup; preserves the existing handoff.

$Function BOOL delivery_reuse_backend(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_fetch

Authenticate the actual owned finalization source before the normal origin fetch.

$Function BOOL delivery_reuse_response(PRIV_TASK)
$Restrict vcl_backend_response

Capture metadata from that source into the existing private native namespace.

$Function STRING reuse_coverage_policy(STRING site, STRING host, STRING scope)
